<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aix-en-Provence</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aquae Sextiae</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aix-en-Provence is a city in Provence, southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, north of Marseille. It was founded in 122 BCE by the Roman consul <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-sextius-calvinus">Gaius Sextius Calvinus</a> as Aquae Sextiae, near the destroyed Salyan stronghold of Entremont, and in 102 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a> defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutones">Teutones</a> nearby. It was later the capital of the counts of Provence and the seat of a parlement, and the painter Paul Cézanne was born there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aix-en-provence.jpg" alt="Aix-en-Provence" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: carlos corzo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aix_en_Provence_-_panoramio_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
